# Array unshift and shift performance

Measures 5,000,000 unshift/shift pairs on one array that holds a single
element, so the workload measures front insertion and front removal without any
resizing: an insertion that claims the free slot before the first element and a
removal that advances the start of the live window. A per-operation regression
such as an extra clone or a type lookup shows up directly. Only the final total
is printed so benchmark output does not dominate execution.

>>> source
let values: int[] = []
let total: int = 0
for (iteration in 0..5000000) {
    values->unshift(iteration)
    let removed = values->shift()
    if (removed != null) {
        total = total + removed
    }
}
print(total)
